WEBVTT

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:12.570
<b>I tried coming alone to our usual park.</b>

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.070
<b>It's a feeling I've never felt.</b>

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:21.660
<b>Like a child, frightened by the sound of the wind</b>

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.670
<b>I ran back along the path home.</b>

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.970
<b>The sky outside the window is too vast. Where are you now?</b>

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.130
<b>Please, may this reach you...</b>

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:44.690
<b>Dear Lord, if you ever grant wishes,</b>

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:50.110
<b>grant my wish right now, please!</b>

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:56.240
<b>I want to hear your voice, I miss you! I want to see you now!</b>

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.830
<b>Why must you already be looking toward tomorrow?</b>

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:06.210
<b>Don't just brush it off, saying the time has slipped by.</b>

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.540
<b>Once more...</b>

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:14.550
<b>I love you, and yet it's been too late since long ago.</b>

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:19.140
<b>Even if I give up, it can't be like the past.</b>

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.350
<b>Don't just decide so simply there's no way, no choice.</b>

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.230
<b>Smile once more.</b>

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:47.250
Everyone is in position.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.480
We're prepared to break in.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.140
Agent Hughes... Your orders, Sir?

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.540
Wait a moment. What is this article?

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.340
This isn't the way I like to do things!

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.050
Next time, wait for my approval.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:02.510
Yes, Sir.

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:05.210
Okay. We'll head in the front door.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:06.980
But...

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:08.150
It'll be fine.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:13.900
Mr. Jones!

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:20.450
Whaddaya want so early?

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:26.200
We're from the NIA. This is Joesph 
Carter Jones's house, correct?

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.330
Yeah... So?

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:32.130
We need to talk. Is he home?

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:37.050
Dunno. Go and check for yourself.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.840
In that case, we'll be happy to.

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:12.210
I don't see him!

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:19.590
Contact the local authorities.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:22.960
Send out pictures of the boy and his 
accomplice to be searched for over a wide area.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:26.360
Cordon off all major roadways and 
stake out checkpoints at all the interchanges!

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:28.650
Seal off Center City!

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.360
I'm home!

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.280
Oh, Joey!

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.110
You were out quite late.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.230
Yeah, well...

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.140
So how'd it go, you little bugger!

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.990
How'd it go?

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:56.690
Don't play dumb!

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.300
You were out on a date, right?

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.680
Had a lot of fun all night long, did we?

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:02.920
Oww!

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:07.640
You two sure get along.

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:10.440
Grandma, that's not it!

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:15.710
She's got me in a headlock!

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.280
Good night...

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:27.980
Lina.

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:44.080
Hello. This is the Jones residence...

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:47.240
<i>Joey, is that you? It's Alan Smithee.</i>

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:48.680
Professor Denton?

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:50.970
Oh, Alan, right!

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:51.970
What's up?

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:55.080
You see, tomorrow's the date!

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.490
That's the emergency evacuation code!

00:04:57.490 --> 00:04:58.950
<i>Did you hear me?</i>

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:01.940
R-Right! So, where's the party at?

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:04.410
<i>The movie opens in October.</i>

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:07.080
<i>Oh, and this is off-the-record.</i>

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:08.220
<i>Got it?</i>

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:08.870
Right.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:12.290
So, please try to avoid being seen by anyone.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:15.370
You wouldn't want to bother the other 
people in the neighborhood, right?

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:45.400
Sis! Hey, Sis!

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:52.700
What's all the racket about?

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.700
Sis, I have something important 
I need to talk about.

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:19.270
Beware of Global Warming!

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:23.740
Eliminate greenhouse gases, 
and protect our Earth!

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:26.610
Thank you. I'm heading out, Sis.

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:26.610
The glaciers and north pole are melting!

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:28.250
And the temperature is going up!

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:29.450
The sea level is also rising!

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:40.460
Looks like you made it here safely.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:43.360
Professor Denton! Psy, too!

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:46.790
Do you understand the situation?

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:50.720
Your phone call was the emergency 
evacuation code, but...

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.430
Yeah, that worked pretty well.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:56.430
I'm sure the people on the 
wiretaps are totally confused.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:59.740
There was a car parked outside as well.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:01.770
Did something happen?

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:05.320
It started with the out-of-control 
robot incident yesterday.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.770
Then, that was...

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:11.200
Your connection to Heroman has 
been revealed to the government.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.360
I bet they've been investigating 
for quite a while.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:18.000
So that's why they set 
up that bogus accident!

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.250
Well, that's that.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:23.380
Whoa there, buddy! What 
are you talking about?

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:28.210
The out-of-control robot yesterday, and 
the building accident were both set-ups!

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:31.670
All for the purpose of uncovering 
Heroman's true identity.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.070
Um, Professor Denton...

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:38.730
Why don't we explain the circumstances 
to the people from the government?

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:39.720
If we do that, then...

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:40.920
It's no use.

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:43.950
If they were interested in talking, then 
they wouldn't have put out this report.

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:45.560
Report?

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:48.270
I guess someone didn't watch the news.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:55.090
According to the report on 
the out-of-control robot,

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:57.530
Heroman attacked the 
reconstruction equipment.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:03.100
They covered it up as the robot 
counterattacking and driving away Heroman.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.880
They seriously made out 
Heroman to be the bad guy.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.500
Oh, no!

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:13.760
Give me a break! It's all 
the government's damn plot!

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:15.590
This isn't right!

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:18.820
Heroman didn't do anything bad!

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.670
This isn't child's play.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:30.360
The government has officially labeled 
Heroman as a remnant of the Skrugg.

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:35.660
What should I do now?

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.390
You should leave the city.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:43.900
The government goons are probably pulling 
out all the stops to capture you and Heroman.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:46.360
You have to get away from here as quickly as-

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.300
You've got to be kidding me!

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:51.920
Joey saved Center City from the Skrugg!

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.200
He's a hero!

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:57.180
So what were we fighting for then?

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:59.680
I don't even know anymore!

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:02.170
There is still a chance to escape!

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:04.870
Or rather, I'd like to believe there is.

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:07.310
What's with the uncertainty?

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:11.070
I don't want to leave this city.

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:13.080
I know how you feel.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:15.760
But if you're caught here, it's game over.

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:17.410
If you can at least escape,

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:20.030
you can find a way to prove your innocence!

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.170
There's no other way right now.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:28.210
Understand, Joey?

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:36.800
Ah, sure I get it.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.730
So we all up and skedaddle?

00:09:41.270 --> 00:09:43.260
We're in this together, after all.

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:45.180
Wait, you can't!

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:49.310
Come on, Joey. Don't make 
me say it twice, sheesh.

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:53.230
Psy...

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:56.860
Then, shall we go?

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:18.840
What are we going to do now?

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:21.960
I have an eccentric scientist friend of mine.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:24.520
He hates other people 
and lives like a hermit.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:28.040
He's the perfect person to hide out with.

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:30.060
Well, if he's a friend of yours...

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:33.650
He lives deep in the mountains of Nevada.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:36.190
We've got to run away there somehow.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:42.350
So to do that we have 
to bust out of Center City

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:45.520
while it's being staked 
out from top to bottom.

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:06.980
What's with this?

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:09.890
Don't complain. It's orders 
from the government.

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:13.600
Our reporting and investigation was perfect!

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:15.710
So why are they saying something like this?

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:18.020
I'm sure it's something very important.

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:20.770
We're talking about aliens here, after all.

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:24.060
I... don't like this.

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:26.030
Well, neither do I.

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:28.290
Is that really how you feel?

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:30.560
Yeah, of course I do.

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:36.140
It makes me shiver seeing how they've 
twisted that footage I shot of the truth.

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:43.350
The truth, huh?

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:54.650
Just so you know, I ain't talkin'.

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:58.020
But before we get to that, would you 
mind explaining what's going on?

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:00.900
Holly Jones, the boy's older sister.

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:04.550
You've only recently returned to Center City.

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:08.420
It seems like you were living in New 
York trying to be a musician beforehand.

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:10.790
How do you know all that?

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:16.830
You're quite the easy one to read.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:24.180
Do you know anything about Joey's secret?

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:25.610
Secret?

00:12:25.610 --> 00:12:27.010
What are you talking about?

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:30.970
I see. Then, on to the next question.

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:33.800
What's Joey like?

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:37.200
Just like I asked.

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:40.040
Don't read too much into it. 
Will you tell me about him?

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:47.070
I'm sorry for waking you up 
in the middle of the night.

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:50.580
What time is it?

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:53.040
I can't tell you the details.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:56.400
But I might not be able to 
come back for a little while.

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:58.920
What? Are you going somewhere?

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:03.590
Please take care of Grandma, okay?

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:06.010
Joey...

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:07.720
You're...

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:10.880
There's not much time. I have to go.

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:14.330
Is there anything I can do?

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:18.480
Thanks. But I don't want to get you involved.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:21.610
You're my little brother. 
What's with all the secrets?

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:28.700
Joey's a good kid.

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:52.840
How is it?

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:56.470
Nope. This road's no good either.

00:13:56.470 --> 00:13:58.850
There are checkpoints everywhere.

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:01.190
Um...

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:04.500
Maybe it'd be better for me to go alone.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:06.240
I can't get everyone involved...

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:08.450
That's not the problem!

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:14.360
Well, it's true that you might be 
able to escape more easily on your own.

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:17.010
But it'd be better to have a car.

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:21.000
And you've got to have your friends 
with you for encouragement, right?

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:24.000
You think you can handle 
this all by yourself?

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.040
Psy...

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:27.010
Prof. Denton...

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:30.530
Professor, we've got to slip 
out of this city somehow.

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:32.890
Yeah, I know!

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:34.960
But, how?

00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:41.130
Well, we'll be needing you 
and Heroman's power for that.

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:44.150
Report.

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:46.650
Right. We have not yet found them.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:51.250
However we have staked out all the highways 
and interstates with checkpoints.

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:53.530
Not a single ant could slip by.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:55.660
That'd be nice if it were true.

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:59.420
We're up against some 
super advanced technology.

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:02.330
We don't know how much of our 
common knowledge will apply.

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:07.200
Joey's older sister didn't know anything.

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:10.170
Which means there's no point in staying here.

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:14.710
I wish I could get ahead 
of them, if it's possible.

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:19.520
Got it? Here's the plan.

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:23.060
All the main roads have checkpoints set up.

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:27.190
First, Joey and Heroman 
cause a distraction here.

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:31.710
If they do that, most of the unit 
in this area should transfer over.

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:35.640
If Heroman appears, there's no reason 
to have the checkpoints anymore,

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:40.160
But just in case we'll make another 
small distraction over here.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:44.860
While they are focused on that, 
we'll break through the checkpoint.

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:48.100
Then Joey wraps things up,

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:50.720
and we meet back up here.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:51.970
Got it.

00:15:57.770 --> 00:15:59.510
Then, let's begin!

00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:00.680
Right!

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:18.700
Heroman... Engage!

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:46.480
Why head toward the mountains?

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:51.190
The Ghost is a mysterious existence 
with powers that we don't understand.

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:55.900
But we do know it has some 
connection with that boy Joey.

00:16:55.900 --> 00:17:00.400
If it's connected to a human, than we can 
use human thinking to predict where it goes.

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:01.410
So then...

00:17:01.690 --> 00:17:04.040
They wouldn't be in a 
city or the coast, right?

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:06.530
There aren't enough places to hide.

00:17:06.530 --> 00:17:11.300
There's also a high probability of involving 
innocent people in battles there.

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:14.630
I think he'd try very hard to avoid that.

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:16.030
Emergency transmission!

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:18.050
The Ghost has been spotted!

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:19.630
Where?

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:21.050
Off Route 6!

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:23.180
In the mountains!

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:34.360
Halt! Halt or we'll shoot!

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:36.950
Idiot! Do you think it understands us?

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:38.450
We've got standing orders to fire at will.

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:40.320
Fire!

00:17:49.570 --> 00:17:51.520
Why'd it turn out like this?

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:14.520
What are you doing? After it!

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:22.780
Go! Hurry!

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:25.030
It's begun.

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:29.400
Professor, is everything set?

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:31.120
Everything's A-OK.

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:34.130
Now, time for us to start, too.

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:41.800
All right, now!

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:48.360
What's this?

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:49.480
It's the enemy!

00:18:52.210 --> 00:18:54.340
How scary!

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:56.020
Run for your lives!

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:07.660
All right!

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:10.190
We've successfully broken 
through the checkpoint!

00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:12.250
Joey, can you hear us?

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:13.270
Yeah!

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:15.670
<i>All that's left is to meet up where we said.</i>

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:16.930
Got it.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:19.800
After him!

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:31.940
Heroman...

00:19:33.350 --> 00:19:34.520
Magnecto!

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:49.490
What the...

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:06.490
All right. That should do it.

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:12.270
Target acquired!

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:14.290
Good! Pursue it!

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:15.520
Don't let them get away!

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:17.400
Heroman, over here!

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:33.990
Should we attack?

00:20:33.990 --> 00:20:35.210
There's no need.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:37.180
We're faster than they are.

00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:39.250
Expand out the personnel on the ground.

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:41.530
Encircle them so they have nowhere to escape.

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:42.460
Roger.

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:44.420
Attention, all personnel!

00:20:44.420 --> 00:20:48.450
The Ghost is currently at 
point 207 heading north!

00:20:49.290 --> 00:20:51.640
There's no end to this...

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:53.060
What should I do?

00:20:55.300 --> 00:20:56.190
That's...

00:20:57.160 --> 00:21:00.720
Damn! It's an abandoned coal mine!

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:08.530
Shoot! We lost them!

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:10.390
Should we land?

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:13.330
It'd be no use, considering who they are.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:15.940
He's probably already vanished.

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:36.990
Joey, welcome back.

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:39.650
Everyone!

00:21:40.390 --> 00:21:42.840
You were pretty late. You had us worried.

00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:45.420
Sorry, a lot of stuff came up.

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:47.280
Well, I'm glad you're okay.

00:21:47.580 --> 00:21:50.580
We don't have much time. Let's 
hurry and get out of here.

00:21:56.800 --> 00:21:58.550
What's the matter, Joey?

00:21:58.550 --> 00:22:01.970
It's nothing! I'm coming.

00:22:29.310 --> 00:22:32.400
<b>I want to get to know you better,</b>

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:35.490
<b>to go at each other with our true feelings.</b>

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:41.830
<b>Your tears and smile are both here.</b>

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:46.260
<b>No matter how hard it is, I won't be scared any more.</b>

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:49.320
<b>With both of us, we can go anywhere.</b>

00:22:49.320 --> 00:22:54.760
<b>Since you're the one who taught me that I'm not alone.</b>

00:22:54.760 --> 00:23:02.450
<b>Every time I mutter the words "I was born to meet you"</b>

00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:07.490
<b>my unease disappears, and my heart burns stronger.</b>

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:14.440
<b>Thank you. We'll go on together with a sign only we understand.</b>

00:23:14.880 --> 00:23:19.300
<b>Carve out this irreplaceable time!</b>

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:23.840
<b>I can't move away from here.</b>

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:28.060
<b>Because I live feeling the same heartbeat.</b>

00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:30.280
<b>I want to protect you to the very last,</b>

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:32.680
<b>to protect the promise built up.</b>

00:23:33.460 --> 00:23:40.080
<b>Thank you. We'll go on together with a sign only we understand.</b>

00:23:40.300 --> 00:23:45.810
<b>We are carving out this irreplaceable time!</b>

00:23:50.930 --> 00:23:53.200
On the next Heroman:

00:23:53.860 --> 00:23:55.860
Professor Denton!

00:23:55.860 --> 00:23:58.160
Psy!

00:23:58.800 --> 00:24:01.270
Under the dogged pursuit of NIA,

00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:05.270
his friends make themselves 
sacrifices, falling out...

00:24:05.870 --> 00:24:08.840
Joey continues to escape, in despair,

00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:10.710
when who else appears but...

00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:15.930
Next time on Heroman #14: Beleaguer!

00:24:15.930 --> 00:24:18.670
Heroman... Attack!
